    "excerpt": "Small Community Air Service Development Program Funder/Agency: Department of Transportation (DOT), Office of the Under Secretary for P...",
    "bodyText": "Small Community Air Service Development Program Funder/Agency: Department of Transportation (DOT), Office of the Under Secretary for Policy Opportunity Number: DOT-OST-2024-0066 Description: The SCASDP program is designed to provide financial assistance to small communities, on a competitive basis, to help them enhance their air service. Grant monies are disbursed to grantees on a reimbursable basis. The goal of this program is to improve air service to underserved communities, including connectivity to the national air transportation system, consistent with statutory requirements and the Department’s strategic goals. The Department may award SCASDP grants to communities to subsidize air service to/from an underserved airport, to an underserved airport to obtain air service to/from that airport, and to an underserved airport to otherwise improve air service. Examples of eligible projects that have received grants include economic air service studies, marketing of air service or an airport, air carrier recruitment, revenue guarantees to air carriers providing air service, start-up cost offsets, fee waivers, reimbursement of air carrier ground handling fees, travel banks. Eligibility: Public entities only, individually or as a part of a consortium Award Details: Total Amount Available: $12,000,000 Deadline: Applications Due July 25, 2024 Opportunity Link Grant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation. Opportunity Title: Reconnecting Communities Pilot (RCP) Program Funder/Agency: Department of Transportation (DOT), 69A345 Office of the... Opportunity Title: Development of Fiscal Year 2025 Commercial Vehicle Safety Plans to Support National Safety Goals Funder/Agency:... Opportunity Title: FY 2024-2026 Wildlife Crossings Pilot Program Funder/Agency: Department of Transportation (DOT), Federal Highway...",
