    "excerpt": "DOE Generation III+ Small Modular Reactor Notice of Intent Informational Webinar Funder/Agency: Department of Energy (DOE), Office of Clean Energy Demonstr...",
    "bodyText": "DOE Generation III+ Small Modular Reactor Notice of Intent Informational Webinar Funder/Agency: Department of Energy (DOE), Office of Clean Energy Demonstrations (OCED) Description: The primary objective of the SMR program is to focus DOE and non-federal resources on a credible and sustainable pathway to fleet-level deployment of Generation (Gen) III+ small modular reactors. To spur the necessary industry-wide momentum, DOE intends to offer funding for projects under this solicitation through two tiers: Tier 1 will provide up to $800M to support up to two first-mover teams of utility, reactor vendor, constructor, and end-users/off-takers committed to deploying a first plant while facilitating a multi-reactor, Gen III+ SMR orderbook. Tier 2 will provide up to $100M to spur additional Gen III+ SMR deployments by addressing key gaps that have hindered the domestic nuclear industry in areas such as design, licensing, supplier development, and site preparation. This webinar will provide additional information about the opportunity including the two tiers, next steps, and resources. Tuesday, July 9, 2024 1 pm. ET Webinar Registration Link Eligibility: Unrestricted Webinar Info Link NOI Info Link Grant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation. Opportunity Title: Rural Energy for America Program (REAP) Funder/Agency: USDA Renewable Energy Systems & Energy Efficiency Improvement... Opportunity Title: Technology Commercialization Fund Open Voucher Call Funder/Agency: Department of Energy (DOE), Office of Technology... Opportunity Title: Military Electric Vehicle (EV) Chargers Funder/Agency: California Energy Commission (CEC) Opportunity Number:...",
