    "bodyText": "DOE Clean Energy Technology Adoption Voucher Opportunities (Reopening & Launch) Funder/Agency: Department of Energy (DOE), Office of Technology Transitions (OTT) Description: The U.S. Department of Energy (DOE) Office of Technology Transitions (OTT), in collaboration with the Offices of Clean Energy Demonstrations (OCED), Fossil Energy and Carbon Management (FECM), and Energy Efficiency and Renewable Energy (EERE), announced the reopening of five voucher opportunities (“VOs”) to accelerate clean energy technology adoption and launch two new VOs with $15 million in available funding to support manufacturers via the Voucher Program. In partnership with ENERGYWERX, DOE offers support to increase adoption readiness of new technologies through selected Voucher Providers (to include National Laboratories and private sector entities) and facilitating the identification and matching of capabilities to Voucher Recipients who need support in overcoming their energy adoption challenges. ENERGYWERX will directly pay the Voucher Provider for the work they have completed to the benefit of the Voucher Recipients. The Voucher Recipient does not receive any funding from DOE nor from the Voucher Provider. Instead, the recipient receives the capability they applied for from the Voucher Providers at no cost. Award Details: Total Amount Available: $15,000,000 Deadline: Applications Due July 09, 2024 Opportunity Link Announcement Link Grant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation. Opportunity Title: Rural Energy for America Program (REAP) Funder/Agency: USDA Renewable Energy Systems & Energy Efficiency Improvement... Opportunity Title: Technology Commercialization Fund Open Voucher Call Funder/Agency: Department of Energy (DOE), Office of Technology... Opportunity Title: Military Electric Vehicle (EV) Chargers Funder/Agency: California Energy Commission (CEC) Opportunity Number:...",
