    "title": "HUD Preservation and Reinvestment Initiative for Community Enhancement (PRICE) - Due 07/10/24",
    "excerpt": "Preservation and Reinvestment Initiative for Community Enhancement (PRICE) Competition Funder/Agency: Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD)...",
    "bodyText": "Preservation and Reinvestment Initiative for Community Enhancement (PRICE) Competition Funder/Agency: Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) Opportunity Number: FR-6700-N-99 Description: HUD has issued a Notice of Funding Opportunity (NOFO) which appropriates $235 million in competitive grant funding for the preservation and revitalization of manufactured housing and eligible manufactured housing communities. Congress has directed HUD to undertake this competition using the Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) statutory and regulatory framework for this first-of-its-kind initiative. PRICE supports communities in their efforts to maintain, protect, and stabilize manufactured housing and Manufactured Housing Communities (MHCs). Of the $235 million available in PRICE funding, $210 million is reserved for the main PRICE competition (PRICE Main). HCD is requesting the maximum award of $75 million under the PRICE Main competition. California-Specific Information: The California Department of Housing and Community Development (HCD) is soliciting public review and comment on its application for the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) Preservation and Reinvestment Initiative for Community Enhancement (PRICE) grant competition. Please submit your written comments to PRICE@hcd.ca.gov. Mailed comments will also be accepted if postmarked no later than June 14, 2024. Comments may be mailed to: Department of Housing and Community Development 2020 W. El Camino Ave Sacramento CA, 95833 Federal Branch Suite 200 Attention: Brad Satterwhite, PRICE Coordinator Eligibility: State and local governmental entities Multijurisdictional Entities Metropolitan Planning Organizations (MPO) Resident-controlled MHCs Cooperatives Non-profit entities (including consortia of non-profit entities) CDFIs Indian Tribes or their Tribally Designated Housing Entities (TDHEs), Tribal non-profits and Native CDFIs Award Details: Total Amount Available: $235,000,000 Deadline: Applications Due July 10, 2024 Opportunity Link Grant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation. Opportunity Title: Rural Energy for America Program (REAP) Funder/Agency: USDA Renewable Energy Systems & Energy Efficiency Improvement... Opportunity Title: ROSS (Resident Opportunity and Self-Sufficiency) Service Coordinator Program - FY2024 - NOFO Funder/Agency: Department... Opportunity Title: Broadband Technical Assistance (BTA) Funder/Agency: Department of Agriculture (USDA), Rural Utilities Service (RUS)...",
