    "bodyText": "Rural Community Development Initiative (RCDI) Funder/Agency: Department of Agriculture (USDA), Rural Housing Service (RHS) Opportunity Number: USDA-RD-HCFP-RCDI-2024 Description: The program is designed to assist qualified private organizations, nonprofit organizations, and public (including Tribal) intermediary organizations, proposing to carry out financial and technical assistance programs to improve housing, community facilities, and community and economic development projects in rural areas. The RCDI program requires the intermediary (Grantee) to provide a program of financial and technical assistance to recipients. The recipients will, in turn, provide programs to their communities (beneficiaries). Eligibility: State and local governmental entities Small businesses For profit organizations other than small businesses Nonprofits Native American tribal governments (Federally recognized) Native American tribal organizations (other than Federally recognized tribal governments) Public and State controlled institutions of higher education Private institutions of higher education Independent school districts Public housing authorities/Indian housing authorities Award Details: Total Amount Available: $5,000,000 Maximum Award: $500,000 Minimum Award: $50,000 Deadline: Applications Due July 10, 2024 Opportunity Link Grant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation. Opportunity Title: Rural Energy for America Program (REAP) Funder/Agency: USDA Renewable Energy Systems & Energy Efficiency Improvement... Opportunity Title: Small Business Innovation Re and Small Business Technology Transfer Programs Phase I Funder/Agency: Department... Opportunity Title: Agrivoltaics Re and Demonstration Funder/Agency: New York State Energy Re and Development Authority...",
