    "bodyText": "Re Training Groups in the Mathematical Sciences Funder/Agency: National Science Foundation (NSF) Opportunity Number: 24-570 Description: The long-range goal of the Re Training Groups in the Mathematical Sciences (RTG) program is to strengthen the nation's scientific competitiveness by increasing the number of well-prepared U.S. citizens, nationals, and permanent residents who pursue careers in the mathematical sciences, be they in academia, government, or industry. The RTG program supports efforts to improve graduate student re training and professional development through structured groups pursuing collaborative re. In addition to graduate student trainees working with faculty members, RTG supported re teams may, but are not required to, include undergraduate or postdoctoral trainees. The RTG program invites submissions in all fields within mathematical sciences; especially encouraged in 2024-2025 are those that align and integrate re in mathematics and statistics with emerging areas such as Artificial Intelligence, Biotechnology, Quantum Computing, and Cybersecurity. Eligibility: Institutions of Higher Education (IHEs) Award Details: Total Amount Available: $12,000,000 Maximum Award: $600,000 Minimum Award: $400,000 Deadline: Applications Due August 13, 2024 Opportunity Link Grant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation. Opportunity Title: Computer and Information Science and Engineering (CISE): Core Programs, Large Projects Funder/Agency: National Science... Opportunity Title: Biodiversity on a Changing Planet (BoCP) Funder/Agency: National Science Foundation (NSF) Opportunity Number: 24-574... Opportunity Title: Technology Commercialization Fund Open Voucher Call Funder/Agency: Department of Energy (DOE), Office of Technology...",
