    "bodyText": "SNAP HFMI 2024 Funder/Agency: Department of Agriculture (USDA), Food and Nutrition Service (FNS) Opportunity Number: USDA-FNS-SNAP-HFMI-2024 Description: The primary purpose of the HFMI project is to develop and test methods to increase the purchase and consumption of qualifying fluid milk by SNAP households by providing them an incentive at the point of purchase at authorized retailer locations. “Qualifying fluid milk” includes all varieties of pasteurized cow’s milk that: Is without flavoring or sweeteners, Is consistent with the most recent dietary recommendations, Is packaged in liquid form, and Contains vitamins A and D at levels consistent with the Food and Drug Administration, State, and local standards for fluid milk. Key Requirement for FY 2024 Applicants: FNS is limiting proposals to project designs that will either: Deliver HFMI incentives as an automatic discount at the point of purchase or Through integration with State Electronic Benefit Transfer (EBT) systems to automatically deposit earned HFMI incentives onto SNAP households EBT cards. Eligibility: Governmental entities (State, local, territory, or tribal agencies) All non-profit organizations Award Details: Total Amount Available: $2,583,428 Maximum Award: $2,583,428 Deadline: Applications Due August 09, 2024 Opportunity Link Grant Management Associates has years of experience with opportunities like this one. Contact us today for a consultation. Opportunity Title: Rural Energy for America Program (REAP) Funder/Agency: USDA Renewable Energy Systems & Energy Efficiency Improvement... Opportunity Title: NINDS Renewal Awards of SBIR Phase II Grants (Phase IIB) for Clinical Trials and Clinical Re (R44 Clinical Trial... Opportunity Title: Small Business Innovation Re and Small Business Technology Transfer Programs Phase I Funder/Agency: Department...",
